  {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": null, "metadata": {}, "outputs": [], "source": ["# Your code/computations here"]},
  {"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["### 3. 🟢 Permutations and Combinations\nCalculate $P(10, 3)$ and $C(10, 3)$ using Python's `math` module. Interpret the difference in terms of selecting features from a pool."]},
  {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": null, "metadata": {}, "outputs": [], "source": ["# Your code here"]},
  {"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["### 4. 🔵 Laplacian Quadratic Form Proof\nProve that for any undirected graph with adjacency $A$, degree $D$, and a node signal vector $\\mathbf{x} \\in \\mathbb{R}^n$, the Laplacian quadratic form satisfies:\n$$\\mathbf{x}^T L \\mathbf{x} = \\frac{1}{2} \\sum_{i,j=1}^n A_{ij} (x_i - x_j)^2$$\nUse this to show that $L$ is positive semi-definite ($L \\succeq 0$)."]},
  {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": null, "metadata": {}, "outputs": [], "source": ["# Your proof here"]},
  {"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["### 5. 🔵 Number of Connected Components\nProve that the number of connected components in an undirected graph is equal to the multiplicity of the eigenvalue 0 in its Laplacian $L$."]},
  {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": null, "metadata": {}, "outputs": [], "source": ["# Your proof/explanation here"]},
  {"cell_type": "markdown", "metadata": {}, "source": ["### 6. 🔵 Spectral Clustering from Scratch\nImplement a simple spectral clustering algorithm. Generate a graph with two clear cliques (using NetworkX's stochastic block model or bipartite graphs), compute the Fiedler vector, partition the nodes by the sign of the Fiedler vector, and check the accuracy."]},
  {"cell_type": "code", "execution_count": null, "metadata": {}, "outputs": [], "source": ["# Your code here"]},
